Program          : DRVEC 0.12
Input Data File  : the .pre files
Output File      : dgate.out
Model            : VARMA-VECM(2,0), M = 2 series, cointegration rank r = 0
Estimation       : Exact Unconditional Maximum Likelihood, Algorithm AS 311 (Mauricio 1997), xi sequence truncated at 1e-3
Transformation   : VECM to stationary VARMA (Mauricio 2006)
Deterministic    : case 3 -- E[nabla Y2] free, E[W] free (drifts as in the .pre files)
Structure        : F diagonal, Theta absent (q = 0), Sigma diagonal
Series           : muskrat mink   (2 in the nabla Y2 block, 0 in Y1)
Sample           : 61 observations from 1851, annual (raw 62)

=============================================================
  OPTIMIZER CONVERGED after 8 iterations
  Objective function = 0.882959103171
  Convergence criterion: norm of scaled gradient <= gradtol
=============================================================

Convergence      : clean convergence, on the scaled gradient
sigma2           :    0.1291281962
logelf           :  -38.9366110727
npar             : 4
AIC              :    1.4077577401   (-2logL + 2k, /n)
BIC              :    1.5461756984   (-2logL + k log n, /n)


=============================================================
  Estimated Parameters and Standard Deviations
=============================================================

  Gamma(L) (nabla Y_t - delta) = alpha (beta'Y_{t-1} - E[W]) + Theta(L) A_t,  delta = E[nabla Y]
  with Pi = alpha beta' of rank r, and beta = [I_r ; beta_2] normalised on Y1.
  Johansen's notation throughout: a NEGATIVE alpha is error-correcting.
  Rows read `equation <- regressor`; D.x is nabla x, A.x its innovation,
  and ec1..ec%d are the equilibrium errors beta'Y_{t-1}.

Parameter                         Estimate    Std.Error   t-stat   p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------

